Your mule is a stupid animal.  It does not even have the sense to drink when there is water.	你的騾子是頭蠢貨。連有水可喝都不懂得喝。
you have no mule, habib, and neither do I.	你沒有騾子，朋友，我也沒有。
Eh?  It is nothing.  A camel I once owned, that is all.	嗯？沒什麼。不過是我曾養過的一頭駱駝罷了。
See how beautifully the pool reflects all around it.  Surely you will wait no longer to drink from it.	瞧這水池映著四周景致，多麼美。你想必不會再猶豫，這就喝上一口吧。
Jabir is very eager for you to drink, yet insists you drink first.  What do your own instincts tell you?	賈比耳一心盼你喝下這水，卻堅持要你先喝。你自己的直覺告訴你什麼？
Perhaps your mule is merely too stupefied to drink.  Perhaps the camel died of old age or injury.	或許你的騾子只是呆得不懂得喝水。又或許那駱駝是因年邁或傷病而死。
Perhaps the camel died of old age or injury.	或許那駱駝是因年邁或傷病而死。
You have a choice between this naturally formed pool and the other pool nearby.  Your own instincts must guide you.	你可以在這座天然水池與附近的另一座水池之間選擇。你得憑自己的直覺判斷。
You need water, but you must rely upon your own instincts to make a decision.	你需要水，但這決定得靠你自己的直覺。
If you wish to use your sword, Arthur, stand on dry land.	亞瑟，你若要拔劍，得先站上乾地。
There is a natural pool of water, surrounded by cliffs and flowing down through a ravine.  Some plants grow here.	這是一座天然水池，四周崖壁環繞，水順著一道溝壑流下。這裡長著些植物。
There is also a camel's skeleton.	這裡還有一具駱駝的骸骨。
Cliffs hide this wadi quite well, and the water flows down from a deep cleft in the ground.	崖壁把這條乾谷藏得極隱密，水便是從地面一道深裂縫中流下來的。
They are strange plants.  I cannot identify them.  Nor do I like the look of them.  They have an odd colour.	這些是些怪異的植物，我認不出是什麼，也不喜歡它們的模樣。顏色透著古怪。
The reflections are almost entrancing.	這倒影幾乎令人看得出神。
Aye, 'tis odd that your mule shows no desire for this water when she is clearly quite thirsty.	正是，你的騾子明明渴得很，卻對這水毫無興致，著實古怪。
The skeleton could be nothing else save a camel.  It must have died here some time ago.	這副骸骨除了駱駝不作他想。想必是很久以前死在此地的。
There are fleas and lice, drying blood and a ripe smell.  There is nothing of any worth.	這裡有跳蚤與蝨子、乾涸的血跡與陣陣腥臭，沒有一樣值得留意的東西。
We are very close to the pool where this water collects.  Follow me.	我們離水匯聚成池的地方不遠了，跟我來。
This trickle of water in the wadi flows into a pool further down.  That is where we wish to go.	這條乾谷裡的細流會匯入下游的一座水池，那正是我們要去的地方。
There is a pool at the end of this wadi.  Follow me.	這條乾谷的盡頭有座水池，跟我來。
We must not waste time with idle chatter, habib.  You must come with me.	我們不能把時間浪費在閒話上，朋友，你得跟我來。
Do not fall into this wadi.  It looks treacherous.	別掉進這條乾谷裡，看來十分凶險。
Not here!  Follow me to the pool.	不是這裡！跟我到水池去。
The side of the wadi is steep and unsafe.  This is not a good place to try to reach the water, but it must flow down to an easier place.	乾谷的側壁陡峭而危險，這裡不是取水的好地方，不過水勢應當會流向更容易抵達之處。
No, no, that is trickier than you think.  Follow me to where you can easily drink from this water.	不、不，這比你想的棘手得多。跟我到能輕易取水的地方去。
Do not try it!  The ground may give way, or you may find yourself unable to climb out.	別輕舉妄動！地面隨時可能塌陷，你也可能爬不出來。
The wadi drops off steeply.  Do not fall into it.	這條乾谷陡然下切，別掉進去。
Water bubbles from the ground and flows down from this wadi.  Be careful you do not fall into it.  You might not be able to climb out again.	水從地下湧出，順著這條乾谷流下。小心別掉進去，你可能爬不出來。
The fissures are not deep, and there is nothing in them.	這些裂縫不深，裡頭什麼也沒有。
You have seen the Pool of Siloam and Hezekiah's aqueduct.  This stream must come from the same source.	你見過西羅亞池與希西家水道，這道水流想必來自同一源頭。
What odd things you babble about.  Clearly, the heat is affecting your brain.	你在胡言亂語些什麼古怪話。想必是這酷熱燒壞了你的腦子。
This seems to be what the Arabs call a wadi, but you are not in a safe place to reach the water.  If you follow it, it should lead to more level ground.	這似乎是阿拉伯人稱作「乾谷」的地形，但你所在之處並不安全，無法取水。若順著它走，應當能通往較平坦的地面。
You have managed to stumble off the crumbling edge and crack open your head upon a rock.                   Wadi shame.	你踩空了崩落的邊緣，一頭撞上岩石，就此喪命。          谷中憾事。
You must follow me this way.  There is a pool of fresh water over here.	你得跟我走這條路，這邊有一池清水。
Ah, your mule lacked the energy to run far.  She waited for you in the small relief offered by the shadow of the cliffs.	啊，你的騾子沒有力氣跑遠，她就在崖壁投下的一小片陰涼裡等你。
Cliffs block your way upon one side and draw close to other cliffs ahead.	崖壁擋住了你一側的去路，前方又與另一片崖壁漸漸逼近。
The tall ridge of cliffs continues unbroken toward some kind of pass or valley ahead.	這道高聳的崖脊連綿不絕，直通向前方某處隘口或山谷。
Aye, there is something sticking out of the ground that looks like the remains of a very ancient wall.	正是，地面上有東西突起，看來像是一道極古老城牆的遺跡。
Your mule has no intention of getting close to a desert cobra.	你的騾子絲毫不想靠近沙漠眼鏡蛇。
Your mule is ready to follow you anywhere except into the valley of the cobras.	你的騾子什麼地方都願意跟你去，唯獨不肯進眼鏡蛇的山谷。
This valley is filled with cobras!   Turn back, Arthur.  You will never pass through here alive.	這山谷裡滿是眼鏡蛇！亞瑟，快回頭，你絕不可能活著穿過這裡。
There are too many cobras to do that without being fatally bitten.	眼鏡蛇太多了，這麼做免不了被咬中要害。
To do that, you would have to get through the cobras.  I can think of no earthly reason to take such a risk.	那樣做，你就得穿過這群眼鏡蛇。我實在想不出有什麼理由值得冒這種險。
Do not trifle with cobras.	別拿眼鏡蛇開玩笑。
The cliffs converge into a narrow valley, but this portion of it is filled with cobras.  And they have no intention of letting you pass.	崖壁在此收攏成一道狹窄的山谷，這一段卻滿是眼鏡蛇，牠們絲毫無意讓你通過。
Your mule is smarter than you.  She refuses to come near the cobras.	你的騾子比你聰明，她拒絕靠近那些眼鏡蛇。
The snake lies where you killed it.	那條蛇倒在你殺死牠的地方。
Beware, Arthur.  This cobra watches you with malign intent.	亞瑟，當心。這條眼鏡蛇正不懷好意地盯著你。
There are some aloe vera plants growing here.	這裡長著幾株蘆薈。
You dare not look long at the glaring sky, unbroken by any cloud, where the sun burns as mercilessly as a demon's eye.	你不敢久望這片無雲的刺目天空，烈日在其中燃燒，猶如惡魔的眼睛般毫不留情。
The cliffs have drawn together to form this narrow valley, but it is impossible to tell whether the valley continues or closes up ahead.	崖壁在此靠攏，形成這道狹窄的山谷，但看不出前方山谷是延續下去，還是就此封閉。
Aye, it is dead and not pleasant to look upon.	正是，牠已經死了，模樣並不好看。
The snakes are alive and well, which you will not be if you get too close to them.	這些蛇活得好好的，你要是靠得太近，可就活不成了。
These snakes are desert cobras and are utterly lethal.  Stay well clear of them.	這些蛇是沙漠眼鏡蛇，致命無比，務必遠遠避開。
A rather novel idea, Arthur, but entirely foolish.	亞瑟，這主意倒是新奇，卻愚蠢至極。
Arthur, beware!  The cobra prepares to strike.	亞瑟，小心！那條眼鏡蛇正準備發動攻擊。
With quick reflexes, you were able to kill the lone cobra, but there are many more.  One of them is bound to strike you.	憑著敏捷的反應，你殺了那條落單的眼鏡蛇，但還有更多蛇在，其中必有一條會咬中你。
Did I not warn you?  This valley may truly be called a dead end, especially for you.	我不是警告過你了嗎？這山谷當真稱得上是條死路，尤其對你而言。
The cliffs reduce to a few boulders as the desert opens up to a trackless expanse.	崖壁漸漸化為幾塊巨石，沙漠隨即展開成一片無路可循的荒野。
As you approach Jerusalem bear in mind that you are one lone foreigner surrounded by dangerous and hostile natives.	你即將接近耶路撒冷，切記你不過是孤身一名異鄉客，身處危險而充滿敵意的當地人之中。
You may, if you wish to return to the Pool of Siloam.	你可以這麼做，若你想回到西羅亞池的話。
At last, after your arduous journey the walls of Jerusalem rise before you.  At this corner you can see the golden mosque called the Dome of the Rock.	歷經艱辛跋涉，耶路撒冷的城牆終於矗立在你眼前。從這個角落，你能望見那座金色的清真寺，人稱「圓頂清真寺」。
Once more you approach the walls of Jerusalem.	你再度接近耶路撒冷的城牆。
This pass brings you to the hill where Jerusalem is built.	這道隘口通向耶路撒冷所在的山丘。
The golden Dome of the Rock is one of the holiest mosques in Islam.  It houses a rock from which the Muslims believe that Mohammed ascended to Heaven.	這座金色的圓頂清真寺，是伊斯蘭教最神聖的清真寺之一。寺內供奉著一塊岩石，穆斯林相信穆罕默德便是由此升天。
I know nothing about it.  Perhaps it is a tower from which the muslims are called to prayer.	我對此一無所知，或許那是穆斯林被召喚禮拜的高塔。
Since you can see the golden mosque, that must be the southeastern corner of Jerusalem.	既然你能望見那座金色清真寺，這裡想必是耶路撒冷的東南角。
As you know, this pass becomes a road which leads you inevitably to the Zion Gate.	如你所知，這道隘口會接上一條路，終將把你引向錫安城門。
There are a number of gates.  It depends on where this pass will lead.	城門不只一座，得看這道隘口通往何處而定。
Let us hope that the mercenaries at the Zion Gate are better disposed toward you this time.	但願這回錫安城門的傭兵們，對你能和善一些。
In addition to Saracens and city soldiers, you may encounter some mercenaries acting as guards.	除了撒拉遜人與城中的士兵之外，你也可能遇上充當守衛的傭兵。
There are some aloe vera plants around.	附近長著幾株蘆薈。
I hope you will pay more attention to Fatima's warnings when you return to pass her Test, as you must yet do.	但願你日後回來接受法提瑪的考驗時，能多留心她的警告——那考驗你終究還得去面對。
By my beard!  This is a cold lesson to learn.  Next time, you must deal more carefully with Fatima before you attempt to leave.	憑我這把鬍子起誓！這教訓可真夠慘痛。下回你想離開之前，得更謹慎地應付法提瑪才是。
It is too dark to see anything.	這裡黑得什麼都看不見。
The water is dark, but not deep.	水色幽暗，但並不深。
It is too dark to see anything above you.	太暗了，看不清你頭頂上方有什麼。
Above you it is solid rock.	你頭頂上方是堅實的岩石。
I see nothing dangerous in here other than the dark.	這裡除了黑暗之外，我看不出還有什麼危險。
The tunnel is small and carved from solid rock, as you can see in the light reflected from the tunnel's mouth.	這條隧道狹小，是從堅實的岩石中鑿出來的——從洞口反射進來的光線便能看清這一點。
The light of the entrance is but a distant point that can barely illuminate this gloom.	入口的光只剩遠處一個小點，幾乎照不亮這片幽暗。
The tunnel is quite dark here.  If you go any further into it, it will be pitch black and dangerous to stumble about in.	這裡的隧道相當昏暗，若再往裡走，便會漆黑一片，在其中摸索行走十分危險。
You cannot see a thing, and you are stumbling dangerously on the roughly hewn rock.	你什麼也看不見，在這粗糙鑿成的岩地上跌跌撞撞，十分危險。
It is pitch black here.	這裡漆黑一片。
It is pure and cold, flowing through this aqueduct from the Spring of Gihon.	這水清澈冰涼，順著這條水道，從基訓泉流淌而來。
The walls of the tunnel are carved from solid rock.	隧道的牆壁是從堅實的岩石中鑿出來的。
It is too dark to think of doing anything.	太暗了，什麼都無從做起。
The tunnel walls offer no grip and the way back up to Fatima is nearly vertical.	隧道牆壁無處可攀，通往法提瑪那邊的回頭路幾乎垂直而上。
You are in a tunnel carved of rock.  There is nothing to climb.	你身處一條鑿於岩石中的隧道，沒有什麼可以攀爬的東西。
Your mule prudently waits for you at the Pool of Siloam.	你的騾子明智地在西羅亞池等你。
That is simple.  The further into the tunnel you go, the darker it will get.	這很簡單。你越往隧道深處走，就會越黑暗。
After a long and dizzying slide you have landed in the cold waters of Hezekiah's Aqueduct.	經過一段漫長而令人暈眩的滑落，你落進了希西家水道冰冷的水中。
It is now pitch black, deep inside the aqueduct.  You are stumbling about dangerously on the roughly hewn floor.	此刻水道深處漆黑一片，你在這粗糙鑿成的地面上跌跌撞撞，十分危險。
Arthur!  What was that sound?	亞瑟！那是什麼聲音？
Ah.  As I feared.  You have struck your head upon a low spot in the tunnel, knocked yourself out, fallen forward into the water and drowned.  Not a very glorious end for the King of all the Britons.	啊，正如我所擔心的。你的頭撞上了隧道裡低矮的一處，昏了過去，往前跌進水中溺斃。對於不列顛眾王之王而言，這算不上什麼光榮的結局。
A fool and his money are soon parted.  Heh, heh, heh!	傻子和他的錢財，總是很快就要分家。嘿嘿嘿！
This is not enough.  All my men must be paid as well.	這還不夠。我手下的人也都得付錢才行。
You may pass, infidel.	你可以過去了，異教徒。
A rich man!!	好個有錢人！！
Now we shall see how well an infidel dies.	這下便讓我們瞧瞧，異教徒是怎麼個死法。
Leaving, heathen?  Good.  We do not like infidels.	要走了嗎，異教之徒？很好，我們不喜歡異教徒。
Come closer, coward!  Our swords thirst for your blood!	靠近點，懦夫！我們的劍渴求你的鮮血！
We do not want your greetings, dog.	我們不需要你的問候，狗東西。
You want me to move, heathen dog?  Give me money and I will consider it.	你要我讓路，異教徒狗？給我錢，我便考慮考慮。
I am not in your way now, but by Allah I will GET in your way if you provoke me.	此刻我沒擋你的路，但憑阿拉起誓，你要是惹惱了我，我便存心擋你的路。
Hah!  Come closer and try that, dog.	哈！有種就靠近點試試看，狗東西。
I do not answer questions, infidel.  Move along.	我不回答問題，異教徒。走開。
You get nothing back from me, unbeliever.  Be on your way.	你從我這裡什麼也得不到，不信者。上路吧。
You will get nothing but trouble if you bother me, heathen dog.	你要是來惹我，異教徒狗，得到的只有麻煩。
We do not buy, we take.	我們不買，我們搶。
What is this?  Some kind of filthy heathen talisman?  Keep it away from me, by Allah.	這是什麼？某種骯髒的異教護符？憑阿拉起誓，離我遠一點。
How can you offer that which you do not have?	你自己都沒有的東西，怎麼拿來給人？
I do not want your wretched mule.	我才不要你那頭可憐的騾子。
Do you fool with me, unbeliever?  I am not amused.	你在耍我嗎，不信者？我可笑不出來。
This is empty, dog!  Give me money or be gone!	這是空的，狗東西！拿錢來，不然就滾！
Do you mock us, infidel?  We are not amused.	你在嘲弄我們嗎，異教徒？我們可笑不出來。
You had better pay in coin, infidel, or you will pay in blood.	你最好用錢來付，異教徒，不然就得用血來償。
If you want to pass, you will come here and pay me.	你若想通過，就過來付錢給我。
I do not waste speech with heathens. Move along, unless you wish to give us more money, heh heh.	我不跟異教之徒多費唇舌。走開，除非你想再多給我們一些錢，嘿嘿。
The Zion Gate is closed.  You cannot enter here.  You must go to the Jaffa Gate.	錫安城門已經關閉，你無法從這裡進去，得走賈法城門才行。
You look like a stinking infidel.  If you want to pass to the Jaffa Gate, you had better make it worth my while.	你看著就是個臭異教徒。想去賈法城門的話，最好讓我覺得值得放你過去。
I do not waste speech with infidels. I would as soon talk to a cur in the street.	我不跟異教徒多費唇舌，跟街上的野狗說話我還更樂意些。
Be on your way, infidel, before we tire of your ugly face.	走開吧，異教徒，趁我們還沒看膩你那張醜臉。
You were warned, infidel!	你已經被警告過了，異教徒！
By Allah! Look, men, our infidel returns as bedraggled as an old sow that has been rolling in dust and muck.	憑阿拉起誓！弟兄們瞧瞧，我們這位異教徒又回來了，狼狽得像頭在塵土泥濘裡打過滾的老母豬。
Hah!  They must raise some clumsy fools where you come from.	哈！你老家想必淨養些笨手笨腳的蠢貨。
Fool of a heathen.  Can you not even find the right gate?	蠢貨異教徒，連該走哪座城門都找不對？
Sheathe your sword, infidel, or we will chop you to pieces.	收起你的劍，異教徒，不然我們把你剁成碎塊。
Be warned, infidel!  Keep your sword sheathed or we will chop you to pieces.	警告你，異教徒！把劍收好，否則我們把你剁成碎塊。
